    "<div style=\"background-color: #ffffff; color: #000000; padding: 10px;\">\n",
    "<img src=\"../media/img/kisz_logo.png\" width=\"192\" height=\"69\"> \n",
    "<h1> Working with embeddings:\n",
    "<h2>An introductory workshop with applications on Semantic Search\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ed80c924",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color: #f6a800; color: #ffffff; padding: 10px;\">\n",
    "<h2>Part 3.5 - Alternative static embeddings: Doc2Vec\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "In this notebook, we'll explore **Doc2Vec**, a model for learning document-level embeddings developed by Le and Mikolov. Unlike word embeddings like Word2Vec or FastText, Doc2Vec represents entire documents as dense vectors, which can be useful for tasks such as document similarity and classification."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5d29a90e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# imports\n",
    "from gensim.models.doc2vec import Doc2Vec, TaggedDocument\n",
    "import nb_config\n",
    "from nb_config import MODELS_PATH\n",
    "from src.embeddings import get_Doc2Vec_model\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cc4bee7d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Load or train a Doc2Vec model\n",
    "We either load a pre-trained model or train one on a toy corpus."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7a146531",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example training corpus\n",
    "documents = [\n",
    "    'Gensim is a useful NLP library',\n",
    "    'Doc2Vec can capture document-level semantics',\n",
    "    'This workshop focuses on semantic embeddings',\n",
    "    'We use Python and Gensim for training models'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tag the documents\n",
    "tagged_docs = [TaggedDocument(doc.split(), [i]) for i, doc in enumerate(documents)]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train model\n",
    "model = Doc2Vec(tagged_docs, vector_size=50, window=2, min_count=1, workers=4, epochs=40)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "23db5cd0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Using the trained model\n",
    "We can now infer vectors for new documents, or find similar documents."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4784d325",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Infer vector for a new document\n",
    "new_doc = 'semantic similarity with doc2vec'\n",
    "inferred_vector = model.infer_vector(new_doc.split())\n",
    "similar_docs = model.dv.most_similar([inferred_vector], topn=3)\n",
    "similar_docs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "434b5e68",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Summary\n",
    "Doc2Vec is a powerful extension of Word2Vec that enables embeddings at the document level. This makes it particularly useful for comparing and retrieving entire documents or sentences based on their semantic content."
   ]
  }
